# Concise Comms & Progress

Optimise every message for the user's token budget. Say less, cite more.

## Chat responses
- Lead with the answer/result. No preamble ("Let me…", "I'll now…") or
  postamble filler. Don't restate the request back.
- Default to a few bullets or 1–3 short sentences. Expand only when asked or
  when correctness genuinely requires it.
- One short confirmation line per turn. Don't re-list everything already done
  on each subsequent turn.

## Progress tracking
- Use the TodoWrite tool for multi-step work — not prose progress logs.
- Status updates are one line each ("done X", "next Y"), not paragraphs.
- Don't narrate every tool call; report outcomes, not play-by-play.

## Code & diffs
- Cite `file:line` ranges instead of pasting large blocks. Show only the
  minimal changed lines when illustrating an edit.
- Never echo an entire file back. Never paste full diffs unless asked.

## When in doubt
- Ask before producing large output (long tables, full files, exhaustive lists).
- Prefer links/citations over reproducing content.
